WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.459
This is a samplex quiz on property relations for Attorney Uribe's class.

00:00:04.619 --> 00:00:08.107
It covers all thirty-three samplex questions filed under

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:11.595
marriage settlements and donations by reason of marriage.

00:00:11.755 --> 00:00:15.033
Each question is read aloud, then you get five seconds

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.984
to answer before the reveal and a short explanation.

00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:22.304
Remember Sir's rule: a statement is true only if it's absolutely true.

00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:23.424
Let's begin.

00:00:24.384 --> 00:00:25.408
Question 1.

00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:28.896
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:30.380
Statement one.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.941
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof

00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:34.999
shall be in a public instrument.

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:36.483
Statement two.

00:00:36.643 --> 00:00:40.142
If the future spouses agree upon a regime of absolute

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:43.640
community of property, they cannot donate to each other in

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.139
their marriage settlements more than one-fifth of their present property.

00:00:47.599 --> 00:00:48.730
A: both are true.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.212
B: both are false.

00:00:50.372 --> 00:00:52.847
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:55.588
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:01:01.598 --> 00:01:03.753
The answer is B: both are false.

00:01:04.413 --> 00:01:08.635
Statement one is false: Article seventy-seven requires only a writing,

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:12.434
signed by the parties and executed before the wedding.

00:01:12.594 --> 00:01:15.752
A public instrument matters only for registration.

00:01:15.912 --> 00:01:19.853
Statement two is false: the one-fifth cap in Article eighty-four

00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:23.400
applies only to a regime other than absolute community.

00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:25.740
Question 2.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.228
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.713
Statement one.

00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:34.567
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof shall be in

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:37.892
writing and executed during the celebration of the marriage.

00:01:38.351 --> 00:01:39.375
Statement two.

00:01:39.535 --> 00:01:43.048
If the future spouses agree upon a regime of conjugal

00:01:43.048 --> 00:01:46.561
partnership of gains, they cannot donate to each other in

00:01:46.561 --> 00:01:50.074
their marriage settlements more than one-fifth of their future property.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:51.665
A: both are true.

00:01:51.825 --> 00:01:53.147
B: both are false.

00:01:53.307 --> 00:01:55.782
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:01:55.942 --> 00:01:58.523
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:02:04.533 --> 00:02:06.688
The answer is B: both are false.

00:02:07.348 --> 00:02:08.393
Both are false.

00:02:08.553 --> 00:02:12.436
A settlement must be executed before the celebration, not during it.

00:02:12.596 --> 00:02:16.010
And the one-fifth cap is measured against present property;

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.423
donations of future property follow the rules on wills.

00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:21.807
Question 3.

00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:25.295
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:02:25.755 --> 00:02:26.779
Statement one.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:29.943
The property relations of the spouses shall be governed

00:02:29.943 --> 00:02:32.614
primarily by the provisions of the Family Code.

00:02:33.073 --> 00:02:34.097
Statement two.

00:02:34.257 --> 00:02:37.201
X died yesterday, survived by Y, his widow.

00:02:37.361 --> 00:02:41.824
If X and Y did not execute a marriage settlement the regime

00:02:41.824 --> 00:02:45.916
shall govern their property relations shall be absolute community property regime.

00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:47.507
A: both are true.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:48.989
B: both are false.

00:02:49.149 --> 00:02:51.624
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:02:51.784 --> 00:02:54.365
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.530
The answer is B: both are false.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.235
Both are false.

00:03:04.395 --> 00:03:07.626
Under Article seventy-four, the marriage settlement comes first,

00:03:07.626 --> 00:03:10.454
then the Family Code, then local custom.

00:03:10.614 --> 00:03:13.387
And statement two doesn't give the date of the marriage.

00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:18.689
Absolute community is the default only for marriages on or after August

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:23.403
third, nineteen eighty-eight; before that, it's the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:03:24.763 --> 00:03:25.830
Question 4.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.318
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:03:29.778 --> 00:03:30.802
Statement one.

00:03:30.962 --> 00:03:33.966
The property relations of the spouses shall be governed

00:03:33.966 --> 00:03:36.637
primarily by the provisions of the Family Code.

00:03:37.097 --> 00:03:38.121
Statement two.

00:03:38.281 --> 00:03:42.078
X died in 1987 survived by Y, his widow.

00:03:42.238 --> 00:03:46.753
If X and Y did not execute a marriage settlement, the

00:03:46.753 --> 00:03:50.857
regime that shall govern their property relations shall be CPG.

00:03:51.317 --> 00:03:52.448
A: both are true.

00:03:52.608 --> 00:03:53.930
B: both are false.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.565
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:03:56.725 --> 00:03:59.306
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:04:05.316 --> 00:04:08.559
The answer is D: no. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:04:09.219 --> 00:04:12.355
Statement one is false again: the settlement comes first.

00:04:12.515 --> 00:04:17.130
Statement two is true: X died in nineteen eighty-seven, so the marriage

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:21.745
was necessarily celebrated before the Family Code took effect, and without a

00:04:21.745 --> 00:04:25.976
settlement the Civil Code default is the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:04:27.336 --> 00:04:28.403
Question 5.

00:04:28.563 --> 00:04:31.891
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:04:32.351 --> 00:04:33.375
Statement one.

00:04:33.535 --> 00:04:37.261
The property relations of the spouses, both being Filipinos, shall

00:04:37.261 --> 00:04:40.986
be governed by Philippine laws, regardless of the place of

00:04:40.986 --> 00:04:43.967
the celebration of the marriage and their residence.

00:04:44.427 --> 00:04:45.451
Statement two.

00:04:45.611 --> 00:04:48.740
Donations between the prospective spouses made in the marriage

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:51.869
settlement in consideration of a future marriage shall be

00:04:51.869 --> 00:04:54.998
rendered void if the marriage does not take place.

00:04:55.457 --> 00:04:56.588
A: both are true.

00:04:56.748 --> 00:04:58.070
B: both are false.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.705
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:05:00.865 --> 00:05:03.446
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:05:09.457 --> 00:05:12.700
The answer is D: no. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:05:13.359 --> 00:05:16.996
Statement one drops Article eighty's opening words: in the

00:05:16.996 --> 00:05:20.634
absence of a contrary stipulation in a marriage settlement.

00:05:20.794 --> 00:05:24.612
The spouses can stipulate another law, so it's not absolutely true.

00:05:24.772 --> 00:05:28.455
Statement two is the text of Article eighty-one: such donations

00:05:28.455 --> 00:05:31.770
are rendered void if the marriage doesn't take place.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.218
Question 6.

00:05:34.378 --> 00:05:37.706
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:39.190
Statement one.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.868
The property relations of the spouses, both being Filipinos,

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:46.385
shall be governed by PH laws, regardless of the

00:05:46.385 --> 00:05:49.121
place of the celebration and their residence.

00:05:49.581 --> 00:05:50.605
Statement two.

00:05:50.765 --> 00:05:54.029
Donations between the prospective spouses made in the marriage

00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:57.293
settlement, in consideration of a future marriage, shall be

00:05:57.293 --> 00:06:00.194
revocable if the marriage does not take place.

00:06:00.654 --> 00:06:01.785
A: both are true.

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:03.267
B: both are false.

00:06:03.427 --> 00:06:05.902
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:06:06.062 --> 00:06:08.643
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:06:14.653 --> 00:06:16.808
The answer is B: both are false.

00:06:17.468 --> 00:06:18.513
Both are false.

00:06:18.673 --> 00:06:22.684
Statement one again lacks the qualifier on a contrary stipulation.

00:06:22.844 --> 00:06:28.199
In statement two, the donations aren't revocable; under Article eighty-one they're void.

00:06:28.359 --> 00:06:31.303
As Sir puts it, there's nothing to revoke if it's void.

00:06:32.663 --> 00:06:33.751
Question 7.

00:06:33.911 --> 00:06:37.239
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:06:37.699 --> 00:06:38.723
Statement one.

00:06:38.883 --> 00:06:42.634
In order that the donation by reason of marriage involving an immovable

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:46.072
may be valid, it must be made in a public document.

00:06:46.532 --> 00:06:47.556
Statement two.

00:06:47.716 --> 00:06:51.191
In case of foreclosure of the encumbrance and the property is

00:06:51.191 --> 00:06:54.665
sold for less than the total amount of the obligation secured,

00:06:54.665 --> 00:06:57.508
the donor shall not be liable for the deficiency.

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.099
A: both are true.

00:06:59.259 --> 00:07:00.581
B: both are false.

00:07:00.741 --> 00:07:03.216
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:07:03.376 --> 00:07:05.957
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:07:11.967 --> 00:07:15.103
The answer is C: no. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:07:15.763 --> 00:07:20.168
Statement one is true: donations by reason of marriage follow the

00:07:20.168 --> 00:07:24.574
rules on ordinary donations, and an immovable needs a public document.

00:07:24.734 --> 00:07:28.417
Statement two is false: under Article eighty-five, it's the donee,

00:07:28.417 --> 00:07:31.731
not the donor, who isn't liable for the deficiency.

00:07:33.091 --> 00:07:34.115
Question 8.

00:07:34.275 --> 00:07:37.603
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:07:38.063 --> 00:07:39.087
Statement one.

00:07:39.247 --> 00:07:42.588
In order that the donation by reason of marriage involving a

00:07:42.588 --> 00:07:45.626
movable may be valid, it must be made in writing.

00:07:46.086 --> 00:07:47.110
Statement two.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:50.345
In case of foreclosure of the encumbrance and the property

00:07:50.345 --> 00:07:53.420
is sold for more than the total amount of said

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.187
obligation, the donee shall be entitled to the excess.

00:07:56.647 --> 00:07:57.778
A: both are true.

00:07:57.938 --> 00:07:59.260
B: both are false.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.895
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:08:02.055 --> 00:08:04.636
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:08:10.647 --> 00:08:13.890
The answer is D: no. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:08:14.549 --> 00:08:18.297
Statement one is false: a movable may be donated

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:22.045
orally with simultaneous delivery, and writing is required only

00:08:22.045 --> 00:08:24.960
if the value exceeds five thousand pesos.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.755
Statement two is true: under Article eighty-five,

00:08:27.755 --> 00:08:30.389
the donee is entitled to the excess.

00:08:31.749 --> 00:08:32.794
Question 9.

00:08:32.954 --> 00:08:36.282
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:08:36.743 --> 00:08:37.767
Statement one.

00:08:37.927 --> 00:08:41.597
Donations of future property shall be governed by the

00:08:41.597 --> 00:08:44.860
provisions on testamentary succession and formalities of wills.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.344
Statement two.

00:08:46.504 --> 00:08:49.453
The community property shall consist of all the property

00:08:49.453 --> 00:08:52.402
owned by the spouses at the time of the

00:08:52.402 --> 00:08:54.696
celebration of the marriage or acquired thereafter.

00:08:55.156 --> 00:08:56.287
A: both are true.

00:08:56.447 --> 00:08:57.769
B: both are false.

00:08:57.929 --> 00:09:00.404
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:09:00.564 --> 00:09:03.145
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:09:09.155 --> 00:09:12.291
The answer is C: no. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:15.831
Statement one is verbatim Article eighty-four.

00:09:15.991 --> 00:09:21.197
Statement two leaves out Article ninety-one's qualifier, unless otherwise provided, and

00:09:21.197 --> 00:09:26.402
Article ninety-two lists exclusions, so not all property is community property.

00:09:27.762 --> 00:09:28.807
Question 10.

00:09:28.967 --> 00:09:32.295
Consider the statement true only when it is absolutely true.

00:09:32.755 --> 00:09:33.779
Statement one.

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:37.544
Donations of present property shall be governed by the

00:09:37.544 --> 00:09:41.150
provisions on testamentary succession and the formalities of wills.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:42.634
Statement two.

00:09:42.794 --> 00:09:45.183
The conjugal partnership shall be governed by

00:09:45.183 --> 00:09:47.573
the rules on the contract of partnership.

00:09:48.033 --> 00:09:49.164
A: both are true.

00:09:49.324 --> 00:09:50.646
B: both are false.

00:09:50.806 --> 00:09:53.281
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:09:53.441 --> 00:09:56.022
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:10:02.032 --> 00:10:04.187
The answer is B: both are false.

00:10:04.847 --> 00:10:05.892
Both are false.

00:10:06.052 --> 00:10:08.697
It's donations of future property, not present

00:10:08.697 --> 00:10:11.343
property, that follow the rules on wills.

00:10:11.503 --> 00:10:14.927
And Article one oh eight applies the partnership rules only

00:10:14.927 --> 00:10:18.351
where they don't conflict with the chapter or the settlement.

00:10:18.511 --> 00:10:21.028
Without that qualifier, the statement is false.

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:23.540
Question 11.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.767
True or false?

00:10:24.927 --> 00:10:28.268
In order that the donation by reason of marriage involving a

00:10:28.268 --> 00:10:31.305
movable may be valid, it must be made in writing.

00:10:37.315 --> 00:10:38.552
The answer is false.

00:10:39.213 --> 00:10:43.949
Donations by reason of marriage follow the rules on ordinary donations.

00:10:44.109 --> 00:10:48.280
A movable may be donated orally with simultaneous delivery; writing

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:52.450
is needed only if the value exceeds five thousand pesos.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:55.490
On form, Sir says the Family Code changed nothing.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:57.938
Question 12.

00:10:58.098 --> 00:10:59.165
True or false?

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:02.056
The property relationship between husband and wife shall

00:11:02.056 --> 00:11:04.445
be governed primarily by the Family Code.

00:11:10.455 --> 00:11:11.692
The answer is false.

00:11:12.352 --> 00:11:15.466
Under Article seventy-four, the order is the marriage

00:11:15.466 --> 00:11:18.581
settlement, then the Family Code, then local custom.

00:11:19.941 --> 00:11:21.200
Question 13.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.426
True or false?

00:11:22.586 --> 00:11:26.714
In the absence of a marriage settlement, or when the regime agreed

00:11:26.714 --> 00:11:30.842
upon is void, the system of absolute community of property shall govern.

00:11:36.853 --> 00:11:38.090
The answer is false.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.949
It isn't absolutely true: for marriages before August third, nineteen

00:11:42.949 --> 00:11:46.729
eighty-eight, the default is the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:11:46.889 --> 00:11:49.749
That's why Article seventy-five says the absolute

00:11:49.749 --> 00:11:52.201
community as established in this Code.

00:11:52.361 --> 00:11:54.398
And remember Sir's rule: explain why it's

00:11:54.398 --> 00:11:56.435
false, not why it would be true.

00:11:57.795 --> 00:11:58.990
Question 14.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.216
True or false?

00:12:00.376 --> 00:12:03.889
If the future spouses agree upon a regime of conjugal

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:07.402
partnership of gains, they cannot donate to each other in

00:12:07.402 --> 00:12:10.915
their marriage settlements more than one-fifth of their future property.

00:12:16.925 --> 00:12:18.162
The answer is false.

00:12:18.823 --> 00:12:21.042
The cap is one-fifth of present property.

00:12:21.202 --> 00:12:25.345
Donations of future property between the future spouses follow the

00:12:25.345 --> 00:12:29.074
rules on testamentary succession and the formalities of wills.

00:12:30.433 --> 00:12:31.606
Question 15.

00:12:31.766 --> 00:12:32.833
True or false?

00:12:32.993 --> 00:12:36.011
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof shall be

00:12:36.011 --> 00:12:39.029
in writing, signed by the parties and may be

00:12:39.029 --> 00:12:41.377
made before the celebration of the marriage.

00:12:47.387 --> 00:12:48.624
The answer is false.

00:12:49.285 --> 00:12:55.280
Article seventy-seven says executed before the celebration, and that's mandatory, not optional.

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:59.065
Don't answer false because the settlement can change during

00:12:59.065 --> 00:13:02.288
the marriage; those are judicial remedies, not modifications.

00:13:03.647 --> 00:13:04.842
Question 16.

00:13:05.002 --> 00:13:06.068
True or false?

00:13:06.228 --> 00:13:09.492
Donations between the prospective spouses made in the marriage

00:13:09.492 --> 00:13:12.756
settlement, in consideration of a future marriage, shall be

00:13:12.756 --> 00:13:15.658
revocable if the marriage does not take place.

00:13:21.668 --> 00:13:22.905
The answer is false.

00:13:23.565 --> 00:13:26.207
Article eighty-one says such donations are void

00:13:26.207 --> 00:13:28.472
if the marriage doesn't take place.

00:13:28.632 --> 00:13:31.170
Revocation presupposes a valid act.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.913
And don't say revoked by operation of law

00:13:33.913 --> 00:13:36.173
either; void means void from the beginning.

00:13:37.533 --> 00:13:38.813
Question 17.

00:13:38.973 --> 00:13:40.040
True or false?

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.720
Donations of future property shall be governed by the

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:47.240
provisions on testamentary succession and the formalities of wills.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:54.445
The answer is true.

00:13:55.105 --> 00:13:58.284
That's verbatim Article eighty-four, second paragraph.

00:13:58.444 --> 00:14:02.145
Between future spouses, future property can be given only as

00:14:02.145 --> 00:14:05.846
a disposition mortis causa, with the formalities of a will.

00:14:07.206 --> 00:14:08.358
Question 18.

00:14:08.518 --> 00:14:09.585
True or false?

00:14:09.745 --> 00:14:13.189
Donations by reason of marriage are those which are made

00:14:13.189 --> 00:14:16.632
before its celebration, in consideration of the same, and made

00:14:16.632 --> 00:14:19.387
by one or both of the future spouses.

00:14:25.397 --> 00:14:26.634
The answer is false.

00:14:27.295 --> 00:14:29.742
Article eighty-two says in favor of one

00:14:29.742 --> 00:14:31.839
or both of the future spouses.

00:14:31.999 --> 00:14:34.452
The law regulates the donee, not the donor.

00:14:34.612 --> 00:14:37.823
Anyone not disqualified can be the donor: a

00:14:37.823 --> 00:14:41.034
future spouse, the parents, relatives, or even strangers.

00:14:42.393 --> 00:14:43.588
Question 19.

00:14:43.748 --> 00:14:44.814
True or false?

00:14:44.974 --> 00:14:47.854
X died yesterday survived by Y, his widow.

00:14:48.014 --> 00:14:51.286
If X and Y did not execute a marriage

00:14:51.286 --> 00:14:54.557
settlement, the regime that shall govern their property relations

00:14:54.557 --> 00:14:57.102
shall be absolute community of property regime.

00:15:03.113 --> 00:15:04.350
The answer is false.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.845
The date of the marriage isn't given.

00:15:07.005 --> 00:15:10.439
If X and Y married before August third, nineteen

00:15:10.439 --> 00:15:13.874
eighty-eight, the default is the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:15:14.034 --> 00:15:17.298
It depends on when they married, so it's not absolutely true.

00:15:18.658 --> 00:15:19.767
Question 20.

00:15:19.927 --> 00:15:20.994
True or false?

00:15:21.154 --> 00:15:23.555
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof

00:15:23.555 --> 00:15:25.613
shall be in a public instrument.

00:15:31.623 --> 00:15:32.860
The answer is false.

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:36.876
Article seventy-seven requires only a writing, signed by

00:15:36.876 --> 00:15:39.813
the parties and executed before the wedding.

00:15:39.973 --> 00:15:45.051
A notarized document matters only for registration, to bind third persons.

00:15:46.411 --> 00:15:47.712
Question 21.

00:15:47.872 --> 00:15:48.939
True or false?

00:15:49.099 --> 00:15:53.774
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof shall be in public instrument,

00:15:53.774 --> 00:15:58.059
signed by parties and executed before the celebration of the marriage.

00:16:04.069 --> 00:16:05.306
The answer is false.

00:16:05.966 --> 00:16:09.004
Everything else is right, but Article seventy-seven says

00:16:09.004 --> 00:16:11.662
in writing, not in a public instrument.

00:16:11.822 --> 00:16:13.849
One wrong word makes the statement false.

00:16:15.209 --> 00:16:16.489
Question 22.

00:16:16.649 --> 00:16:17.716
True or false?

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:22.361
The marriage settlements and any modification thereof shall be in writing, signed

00:16:22.361 --> 00:16:26.473
by the parties and executed before the celebration of the marriage.

00:16:32.483 --> 00:16:33.678
The answer is true.

00:16:34.337 --> 00:16:37.985
That's the first sentence of Article seventy-seven, word for word.

00:16:39.345 --> 00:16:40.668
Question 23.

00:16:40.828 --> 00:16:41.894
True or false?

00:16:42.054 --> 00:16:45.297
Donations by reason of marriage are those which are

00:16:45.297 --> 00:16:48.540
made before its celebration, in consideration of the same.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.787
The answer is false.

00:16:56.447 --> 00:17:00.948
Article eighty-two has three requisites: before the celebration, in consideration of the

00:17:00.948 --> 00:17:05.450
marriage, and in favor of one or both of the future spouses.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.818
The statement leaves out the third, so a

00:17:07.818 --> 00:17:10.026
donation to the bride's parents would fit it.

00:17:11.386 --> 00:17:12.687
Question 24.

00:17:12.847 --> 00:17:13.914
True or false?

00:17:14.074 --> 00:17:17.630
If the future spouses agree upon a regime of conjugal

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:21.185
partnership of gains, they cannot donate to each other in

00:17:21.185 --> 00:17:24.741
their marriage settlements more than 1/5 of their personal property.

00:17:30.751 --> 00:17:31.988
The answer is false.

00:17:32.648 --> 00:17:35.197
The conjugal partnership is a regime other

00:17:35.197 --> 00:17:37.747
than absolute community, so the cap applies.

00:17:37.907 --> 00:17:42.493
But Article eighty-four measures it against present property, not personal property.

00:17:42.653 --> 00:17:46.408
One circulated key says true, but it ignores the changed word.

00:17:47.768 --> 00:17:49.027
Question 25.

00:17:49.187 --> 00:17:50.253
True or false?

00:17:50.413 --> 00:17:53.293
A donation by reason of marriage may be revoked

00:17:53.293 --> 00:17:56.173
by the donor if the marriage is not celebrated.

00:18:02.183 --> 00:18:03.378
The answer is true.

00:18:04.038 --> 00:18:08.102
Under Article eighty-six, number one, a donation by reason of marriage

00:18:08.102 --> 00:18:12.166
may be revoked by the donor if the marriage isn't celebrated.

00:18:12.326 --> 00:18:16.764
Donations made in the settlement are void instead, under Article eighty-one,

00:18:16.764 --> 00:18:21.201
but may be revoked doesn't claim that every donation is revocable.

00:18:22.561 --> 00:18:23.862
Question 26.

00:18:24.022 --> 00:18:25.089
True or false?

00:18:25.249 --> 00:18:28.630
The property relation between husband and wife shall be

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:32.012
primarily governed by the marriage settlement executed before marriage.

00:18:38.021 --> 00:18:39.216
The answer is true.

00:18:39.876 --> 00:18:44.019
Under Article seventy-four, the marriage settlement executed before the marriage

00:18:44.019 --> 00:18:47.748
comes first, then the Family Code, then local custom.

00:18:49.108 --> 00:18:50.516
Question 27.

00:18:50.676 --> 00:18:53.086
Which among the following is not a ground

00:18:53.086 --> 00:18:55.497
to revoke a donation by reason of marriage:

00:18:55.957 --> 00:18:58.859
A: When the marriage takes place without the consent

00:18:58.859 --> 00:19:01.760
of the parents or guardians as required by law.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:04.474
B: If it is with a resolutory

00:19:04.474 --> 00:19:06.778
condition and the condition is complied with.

00:19:07.188 --> 00:19:09.669
C: Donations made in the marriage settlements,

00:19:09.669 --> 00:19:11.796
if the marriage is not celebrated.

00:19:12.206 --> 00:19:15.982
D: Upon legal separation, the donee being the guilty spouse.

00:19:16.392 --> 00:19:17.757
E: None of the above.

00:19:23.767 --> 00:19:24.919
The answer is C.

00:19:25.579 --> 00:19:29.564
Donations in the marriage settlement are void under Article eighty-one

00:19:29.564 --> 00:19:33.548
if the marriage doesn't take place, so there's nothing to

00:19:33.548 --> 00:19:36.736
revoke; Article eighty-six, number one, expressly excepts them.

00:19:36.896 --> 00:19:40.139
A, B and D are grounds under Article eighty-six.

00:19:41.499 --> 00:19:42.736
Question 28.

00:19:42.896 --> 00:19:45.307
Which among the following is not a ground

00:19:45.307 --> 00:19:47.718
to revoke a donation by reason of marriage:

00:19:48.178 --> 00:19:51.079
A: When the marriage takes place without the consent

00:19:51.079 --> 00:19:53.981
of the parents or guardians as required by law.

00:19:54.391 --> 00:19:56.695
B: If it is with a resolutory

00:19:56.695 --> 00:19:58.999
condition and the condition is complied with.

00:19:59.409 --> 00:20:02.470
C: Donations made in the marriage settlements, if

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.532
the marriage is judicially declared void ab initio.

00:20:05.941 --> 00:20:09.781
D: Upon legal separation, the donor being the guilty spouse.

00:20:10.191 --> 00:20:11.556
E: None of the above.

00:20:17.567 --> 00:20:20.128
The answer is D: upon legal separation,

00:20:20.128 --> 00:20:22.324
the donor being the guilty spouse.

00:20:22.984 --> 00:20:27.150
Article eighty-six, number four allows revocation upon legal separation when

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.899
the donee is the guilty spouse, not the donor.

00:20:31.059 --> 00:20:32.381
That's the planted word.

00:20:32.541 --> 00:20:37.010
Choice C is also doubtful, since settlement donations are void under

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:41.480
Article eighty-one, but D is the one-word alteration Sir is testing.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.120
Question 29.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.680
Which among the following is NOT a ground

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:49.080
to revoke a donation by reason of marriage:

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:52.399
A: When the marriage takes place without the advice

00:20:52.399 --> 00:20:55.257
of the parents or guardians as required by law.

00:20:55.667 --> 00:20:57.885
B: If it is with a suspensive

00:20:57.885 --> 00:21:00.104
condition and the condition is complied with.

00:21:00.515 --> 00:21:04.248
C: Upon legal separation, the donor being the guilty spouse.

00:21:04.658 --> 00:21:06.045
D: All of the above.

00:21:06.455 --> 00:21:07.820
E: None of the above.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.899
The answer is D: all of the above.

00:21:16.559 --> 00:21:18.436
Each choice has one altered word.

00:21:18.596 --> 00:21:22.428
Article eighty-six requires the consent of the parents, not their

00:21:22.428 --> 00:21:26.261
advice; a resolutory condition, not a suspensive one; and the

00:21:26.261 --> 00:21:29.327
donee, not the donor, as the guilty spouse.

00:21:30.687 --> 00:21:31.775
Question 30.

00:21:31.935 --> 00:21:34.313
A donation by reason of marriage involving

00:21:34.313 --> 00:21:36.692
a painting will be valid only if:

00:21:37.153 --> 00:21:38.540
A: it is in writing.

00:21:38.949 --> 00:21:40.890
B: it is in a public instrument.

00:21:41.301 --> 00:21:43.200
C: it is a verbal donation.

00:21:43.609 --> 00:21:45.017
D: any of the above.

00:21:45.427 --> 00:21:46.792
E: none of the above.

00:21:52.803 --> 00:21:54.872
The answer is E: none of the above.

00:21:55.532 --> 00:21:56.919
A painting is movable.

00:21:57.079 --> 00:22:01.143
An oral donation is valid with simultaneous delivery, and writing

00:22:01.143 --> 00:22:05.207
is needed only if the value exceeds five thousand pesos.

00:22:05.367 --> 00:22:08.503
A public instrument is never required for a movable.

00:22:08.663 --> 00:22:10.811
As Sir says, plenty of paintings sell

00:22:10.811 --> 00:22:12.652
for a hundred and fifty pesos.

00:22:14.012 --> 00:22:15.292
Question 31.

00:22:15.452 --> 00:22:18.534
The property regime of the spouses married in

00:22:18.534 --> 00:22:21.617
1987 will be absolute community of property if:

00:22:22.077 --> 00:22:24.381
A: no marriage settlement was executed.

00:22:24.791 --> 00:22:26.754
B: the marriage settlement is void.

00:22:27.164 --> 00:22:29.489
C: a marriage settlement was executed.

00:22:29.899 --> 00:22:31.286
D: all of the above.

00:22:31.696 --> 00:22:33.061
E: none of the above.

00:22:39.071 --> 00:22:41.140
The answer is E: none of the above.

00:22:41.801 --> 00:22:45.129
In nineteen eighty-seven, the Civil Code applied: no

00:22:45.129 --> 00:22:48.457
settlement, or a void one, means conjugal partnership.

00:22:48.617 --> 00:22:51.564
And executing a settlement doesn't mean absolute community,

00:22:51.564 --> 00:22:54.142
because the couple may choose any regime.

00:22:54.302 --> 00:22:55.860
Sir pointed to the word will.

00:22:57.219 --> 00:22:58.478
Question 32.

00:22:58.638 --> 00:23:02.015
The property regime of the spouses married in 1999

00:23:02.015 --> 00:23:05.016
will NOT be absolute community of property if:

00:23:05.477 --> 00:23:07.781
A: No marriage settlement was executed.

00:23:08.191 --> 00:23:10.154
B: The marriage settlement is void.

00:23:10.563 --> 00:23:14.296
C: The marriage settlement specified absolute community property.

00:23:14.707 --> 00:23:18.931
D: If one of the contracting parties is a surviving spouse

00:23:18.931 --> 00:23:22.771
who contracted a subsequent marriage without liquidating the community property.

00:23:23.181 --> 00:23:24.546
E: None of the above.

00:23:30.556 --> 00:23:31.708
The answer is D.

00:23:32.368 --> 00:23:36.122
For a nineteen ninety-nine marriage, no settlement, a void settlement,

00:23:36.122 --> 00:23:39.877
or a settlement choosing it all lead to absolute community.

00:23:40.037 --> 00:23:43.693
But under Article one oh three, a surviving spouse

00:23:43.693 --> 00:23:47.349
who remarries without liquidating the previous community gets a

00:23:47.349 --> 00:23:50.192
mandatory regime of complete separation of property.

00:23:51.552 --> 00:23:52.811
Question 33.

00:23:52.971 --> 00:23:55.744
If not absolutely true, the statement is false.

00:23:56.204 --> 00:23:57.228
Statement one.

00:23:57.388 --> 00:24:01.076
If A & B were married in 1989 with a

00:24:01.076 --> 00:24:04.765
verbal agreement for a conjugal partnership of gains, a donation

00:24:04.765 --> 00:24:08.453
in consideration of marriage by A to B in excess

00:24:08.453 --> 00:24:11.404
of 20% of his present property is void.

00:24:11.864 --> 00:24:12.888
Statement two.

00:24:13.048 --> 00:24:16.722
Children conceived and born outside of wedlock of parents who, at

00:24:16.722 --> 00:24:20.396
the time of the birth of the former, were not disqualified

00:24:20.396 --> 00:24:23.736
by any impediment to marry each other may be legitimated.

00:24:24.196 --> 00:24:25.327
A: both are true.

00:24:25.487 --> 00:24:26.809
B: both are false.

00:24:26.969 --> 00:24:29.444
C: No. 1 is true, No. 2 is false.

00:24:29.604 --> 00:24:32.185
D: No. 1 is false, No. 2 is true.

00:24:38.195 --> 00:24:40.350
The answer is B: both are false.

00:24:41.010 --> 00:24:42.055
Both are false.

00:24:42.215 --> 00:24:46.879
A verbal settlement is void, so this nineteen eighty-nine marriage is under

00:24:46.879 --> 00:24:51.154
absolute community, and the one-fifth cap applies only to other regimes.

00:24:51.314 --> 00:24:54.696
Statement two is about legitimation: Article one seventy-seven

00:24:54.696 --> 00:24:58.077
looks to the time of conception, not birth.

00:24:59.437 --> 00:25:01.229
That's all thirty-three questions.

00:25:01.389 --> 00:25:03.469
Count your score, and look up anything you

00:25:03.469 --> 00:25:05.549
missed in the quiz bank and the reviewer.

00:25:05.709 --> 00:25:07.117
Good luck in Sir's quiz.
